+
+## Usage reported to `afterModelResponse`
+
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and its `totalUsage` argument is the componentwise sum of the usage every provider call in the turn reported, so a turn that ran tools reports the cost of all of them and not only the last leg ([validated by: reports usage covering every provider call of a two-tool-round turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+- The hook also receives `roundUsage`, one `UsageMetadata` per provider call that reported usage, in call order, so a consumer that wants provider-call granularity keeps it; the argument names themselves say the total is a sum, so a reader never has to open the orchestrator to learn what the number is ([validated by: reports usage covering every provider call of a two-tool-round turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+- A round whose provider reported no usage contributes nothing rather than poisoning the total: the rounds that did report are still summed, never `undefined` or `NaN` ([validated by: still counts the rounds that reported usage when some rounds report none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- A turn where no round reported usage still reports nothing: `totalUsage` is `undefined` and `roundUsage` is empty ([validated by: reports nothing when no round of the turn reported usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L122)).
+- A turn that ran no tools reports exactly what it reported before this change: one provider call is its own sum, and its breakdown lists that call alone ([validated by: reports exactly what a no-tool turn reports today](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L139)).
